<div class="section-card">
  <div class="section-header">
    <h2>Explanation of Recoil</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-content">
    <p>When a gun fires a bullet, a series of events occur governed by Newton's Third Law:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Action:</b> The gun exerts a force on the bullet, accelerating it forward. This is the "action."</li>
      <li><b>Reaction:</b> Simultaneously, the bullet exerts an equal and opposite force back on the gun. This is the "reaction."</li>
      <li><b>Result:</b> Because the gun is much heavier than the bullet, the gun's acceleration (recoil) is much smaller than the bullet's acceleration. However, the forces are equal in magnitude.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

